  "response": "## Analyse\n\nJe dois créer `tests/test_summarize.py` avec 4 tests couvrant les cas limites (texte vide, court, long, max_sentences=1). Avant de générer, je nettoie tout fichier partiellement existant et je valide la syntaxe + la collecte pytest après génération.\n\n**Étapes** :\n1. Nettoyer `tests/test_summarize.py` s'il existe\n2. Générer le fichier avec 4 tests robustes\n3. Valider : compilation Python + collecte pytest + exécution\n\n---\n\n```python path: tests/test_summarize.py\n\"\"\"Tests for tools/summarize.py\"\"\"\nimport pytest\nfrom tools.summarize import summarize, split_sentences, score_sentence\n\n\nclass TestSplitSentences:\n    \"\"\"Test split_sentences function.\"\"\"\n    \n    def test_empty_text(self):\n        \"\"\"Empty text returns empty list.\"\"\"\n        result = split_sentences(\"\")\n        assert result == []\n    \n    def test_single_sentence(self):\n        \"\"\"Single sentence without period.\"\"\"\n        result = split_sentences(\"Hello world\")\n        assert len(result) >= 1\n    \n    def test_multiple_sentences(self):\n        \"\"\"Multiple sentences are split correctly.\"\"\"\n        text = \"First sentence. Second sentence. Third sentence.\"\n        result = split_sentences(text)\n        assert len(result) >= 2\n\n\nclass TestScoreSentence:\n    \"\"\"Test score_sentence function.\"\"\"\n    \n    def test_score_non_empty(self):\n        \"\"\"Score is computed for non-empty sentence.\"\"\"\n        score = score_sentence(\"This is a test sentence\")\n        assert isinstance(score, (int, float))\n        assert score >= 0\n\n\nclass TestSummarize:\n    \"\"\"Test summarize function.\"\"\"\n    \n    def test_empty_text(self):\n        \"\"\"Empty text returns empty string.\"\"\"\n        result = summarize(\"\")\n        assert result == \"\"\n    \n    def test_short_text_less_than_max_sentences(self):\n        \"\"\"Text shorter than max_sentences returns original.\"\"\"\n        text = \"First sentence. Second sentence.\"\n        result = summarize(text, max_sentences=5)\n        # Result should be non-empty and contain original content\n        assert len(result) > 0\n        assert \"sentence\" in result.lower()\n    \n    def test_long_text_summarized(self):\n        \"\"\"Long text is summarized to max_sentences.\"\"\"\n        text = \". \".join([f\"Sentence {i}\" for i in range(10)]) + \".\"\n        result = summarize(text, max_sentences=3)\n        # Result should be shorter than original\n        assert len(result) <= len(text)\n        # Should contain at least one sentence\n        assert len(result) > 0\n    \n    def test_max_sentences_one(self):\n        \"\"\"max_sentences=1 returns single sentence.\"\"\"\n        text = \"First sentence. Second sentence. Third sentence.\"\n        result = summarize(text, max_sentences=1)\n        # Result should be non-empty\n        assert len(result) > 0\n        # Should be shorter than original\n        assert len(result) <= len(text)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Validation\n\n```bash\n# Nettoyer avant génération\nrm -f tests/test_summarize.py\n\n# Valider syntaxe\npython -m py_compile tests/test_summarize.py\n\n# Collecter les tests\npytest tests/test_summarize.py --collect-only -q\n\n# Exécuter les tests\npytest tests/test_summarize.py -v --tb=line\n```\n\n**Résultat attendu** : 7 tests collectés et tous passent ✓",
